From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 02:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ppc: fix HI/LO_WORD_OFFSET endian selection on Darwin

The guard "#if __FLOAT_WORD_ORDER == __LITTLE_ENDIAN" uses glibc
<endian.h> macros that do not exist on Darwin. In the preprocessor,
undefined identifiers evaluate to 0, so the comparison becomes 0 == 0
and the LITTLE-endian word layout is silently selected on big-endian
Darwin. Every ConvertIntToFloatingPointNoPPC64 emission then stores the
high word of the constructed double at offset 4 and the low word at
offset 0, so lfd assembles garbage denormals out of both the 2^52 bias
constant and the value.

Observed effect: any Smi argument reaching an ieee754/fmod C call
turned to garbage (Math.sin(1)/pow(2,3) -> NaN or denormal junk,
5.5 % 2 -> 0), while HeapNumber arguments (loaded with lfd, no
conversion) were computed perfectly - confirmed by disassembling the
emitted Builtins_MathPow from embedded.S. The npm6 build failure traces
to the same root: internal/crypto/random.js computes 2**32-1 through
the broken runtime pow at module load, making kMaxPossibleLength
negative so every randomBytes() throws ERR_OUT_OF_RANGE.

On Linux the glibc macros are defined and the guard picks the correct
branch, which is why the same patchset worked on ppc32 Linux. Test with
V8's own V8_TARGET_BIG_ENDIAN (driven by the V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC_BE
build define) instead.
---
--- a/deps/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
+++ b/deps/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
@@ -26,12 +26,17 @@
 
 #include <iostream>
 
-#if __FLOAT_WORD_ORDER == __LITTLE_ENDIAN
-#define LO_WORD_OFFSET 0
-#define HI_WORD_OFFSET 4
-#else
+// Word offsets of an IEEE double stored to memory. Must be tested with V8's
+// own endianness macros: __FLOAT_WORD_ORDER/__LITTLE_ENDIAN are glibc-isms
+// that are simply undefined on Darwin, where an #if comparing them becomes
+// 0 == 0 and silently selects the little-endian layout on a big-endian
+// target (garbage denormals out of every int-to-double conversion).
+#if defined(V8_TARGET_BIG_ENDIAN)
 #define LO_WORD_OFFSET 4
 #define HI_WORD_OFFSET 0
+#else
+#define LO_WORD_OFFSET 0
+#define HI_WORD_OFFSET 4
 #endif
 
 // Satisfy cpplint check, but don't include platform-specific header. It is
-- 
2.39.5
